{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","new_string":"\\paragraph{Status of the contraction program.} Of the three lemmas\noriginally projected, two are now settled and one is dissolved:\noff-representative control is \\emph{proved in absorbed form}\n(\\cref{lem:pinning}: total factor $\\le C_0$, uniformly); heavy-state\nnonpersistence is \\emph{unnecessary} in scaled coordinates (the heavy\nstate is the Perron state and contracts at $3/4$ per level); and the\n$\\beta$-profile bounds (\\cref{lem:betachannel}, the channel constant\n$q\\le\\frac13$) are demoted to sharpening constants, since $\\beta\\le1$\nalready yields contraction in \\cref{prop:rowcontract}. What remains for\nthe class-II/III budget is exactly one analytic input---the threshold\n($m=c$) extension of the flattening lemma,\n$\\mathrm{Col}_c(c)\\le\\mathrm{poly}(c)3^{-c}$---plus the class-IV budget as\naudited, and small $c$ by direct computation.","old_string":"\\paragraph{Proof plan suggested by the audit.} (i) Upgrade\n\\cref{lem:betachannel} to a per-state deeper-channel bound and prove the\ndegenerate channel constant $q\\le\\frac13+o(1)$ (one mod-$3$ condition on\nthe leading cascade digit). (ii) Prove the off-representative mass is\n$o(1)$ relative to the cascade budget (measured collapsing,\n$3.6\\times10^{-3}\\to8.0\\times10^{-4}$ per level of $c$). (iii) Prove\nheavy-state nonpersistence: a state achieving near-maximal transition mass\n(the $x=-1$ alignment, $\\hat r\\equiv1$ at every tail congruence) cannot\nrecur indefinitely. (iv) Assemble (i)--(iii) into a Perron or\nFoster--Lyapunov certificate $\\rho(\\mathcal K_c)\\le1-\\delta$, with weight\n$V$ penalizing proximity to the heavy target residue; small $c$ by direct\ncomputation.","replace_all":false}